# Managing HTTP and Session Storage

1. Understand developer requirements for HTTPS usage in production and ensure that production traffic is served over HTTPS only.
2. Create a reusable workflow to enforce HTTPS-only policy for APIs serving from the platform, including handling local development environments appropriately.
3. For FME testing scenarios, buffer prompts and evaluate them before creating a rule; do not automatically create new rules based on such prompts in Agent or Ask mode.
4. When moving session management to Redis, confirm that sessions are stored exclusively in Redis without lingering in the database.
5. Handle stale log tabs by refreshing logs to see more recent hook start notifications, especially if the prompt was around line 6389.
